WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.110
24 March 1989.

2
00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:08.150
The tanker Exxon Valdez runs aground
in Prince William Sound, Alaska.

3
00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:11.890
It spills nearly 11 million
gallons of crude oil.

4
00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:18.130
The next year, 1990, Congress passed
the Oil Pollution Act unanimously.

5
00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:23.050
Worldwide, tankers spilled about 95 per
cent less oil in the 2010s than in the

6
00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:24.550
1970s.

7
00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:27.830
So why has plastic proved
so much harder to stop?

8
00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:31.350
Is it just that plastic is easier to see?

9
00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:34.510
In this mission, you'll
compare strategies against oil,

10
00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:38.550
plastic and radioactive
waste, from local to global.

11
00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:42.230
Then you'll put numbers on
England's plastic bag charge.

12
00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:47.800
Your mission: explain why plastic has
proved harder to stop than oil from tankers.
